erly aggressive. It’s a good fit for vinyl owners who want dependable cleaning with simple day-to-day maintenance.</p><p><a href="/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-CC-Plus">Read the full review</a> or <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00Q8M0NWE?tag=scorpiusllc-20">check current pricing</a>.</p></div><div class="d-flex gap-2 mt-4"><a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="/reviews/Dolphin-Nautilus-CC-Plus">Read Full Review</a><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B00Q8M0NWE?tag=scorpiusllc-20" target="_blank" class="btn btn-warning fw-bold ">Check Price on Amazon</a></div></div></div></div></div><div id="review-Hayward-SharkVac-XL" class="card mb-4"><div class="row g-0"><div class="col-md-4 text-center p-4 d-flex align-items-center justify-content-center bg-white"><img src="https://commerce.hayward-pool-assets.com/magento/2026/RC9742WCCUBY/sharkvac_xl_left_3434.png" class="img-fluid rounded-start" alt="Hayward SharkVac XL" style="max-height:200px;object-fit:contain"/></div><div class="col-md-8"><div class="card-body"><div class="d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start"><div><h3 class="card-title h4">Hayward SharkVac XL</h3><span class="badge bg-primary mb-2">Best Simple Vinyl Pick</span></div><div class="text-end"><div class="h4 mb-0 text-primary">$<!-- -->1599</div></div></div><div class="card-text mt-3">Features smart steering technology for an efficient cleaning pattern and a large debris container.</div><p class="card-text"><strong>Why we picked it:</strong></p><div class="card-text"><p>A practical option if you want straightforward floor-focused cleaning with predictable operation. It’s a good choice when your liner pool’s main need is consistent floor pickup.</p><p><a href="/reviews/Hayward-SharkVac-XL">Read the full review</a> or <a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07SR4M42F?tag=scorpiusllc-20">check current pricing</a>.</p></div><div class="d-flex gap-2 mt-4"><a class="btn btn-outline-primary" href="/reviews/Hayward-SharkVac-XL">Read Full Review</a><a href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B07SR4M42F?tag=scorpiusllc-20" target="_blank" class="btn btn-warning fw-bold ">Check Price on Amazon</a></div></div></div></div></div></div><div class="row mt-5"><div class="col-lg-8 mx-auto"><div class="card border-primary"><div class="card-header bg-primary text-white"><h3 class="h5 mb-0">Buying Advice</h3></div><div class="card-body"><h3>Vinyl Liner Buying Advice</h3><p>For vinyl pools, prioritize stable traction and a design you’ll actually maintain. If your pool is large, ensure you have enough runtime to finish a full cycle. If your pool gets heavy leaves, choose larger debris capacity. And if you care about waterline cleaning, confirm the robot’s wall behavior is reliable.</p><h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3><p><strong>Are robotic pool cleaners safe for vinyl liners?</strong><br>Most are, but choose models known for stable traction and avoid overly aggressive brush behavior.</p><p><strong>Is heavier always better on vinyl?</strong><br>No. Weight can improve traction, but vinyl owners should prioritize balance and predictable movement.</p></div></div></div></div></div></main><footer class="bg-dark text-white text-center py-3 mt-auto"><div class="container"><p class="mb-1">© <!-- -->2026<!-- --> <!-- -->The Pool Lab<!-- -->. All rights reserved.</p><small class="text-white-50">The Pool Lab<!-- --> is a participant in the Amazon Services LLC Associates Program, an affiliate advertising program designed to provide a means for sites to earn advertising fees by advertising and linking to Amazon.com.</small></div></footer><script src="/_next/static/chunks/webpack-9104c05f1a1687bc.js" crossorigin="" async=""></script><script>(self.__next_f=self.__next_f||[]).push([0]);self.__next_f.push([2,null])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"1:HL[\"/_next/static/css/d071dca61fbb01bf.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n2:HL[\"/_next/static/css/0fc6c400c3ed5371.css\",\"style\",{\"crossOrigin\":\"\"}]\n0:\"$L3\"\n"])</script><script>self.__next_